{"prompt": "My flight got cancelled and I have a meeting in Berlin tomorrow morning. What do I do?", "response": "Let's fix this step by step. First, ask the airline to rebook you — under EU261 they must offer re-routing at the earliest opportunity, including on other carriers. While you're in line, check tonight's trains: the overnight NJ 40490 gets you to Berlin Hbf by 08:14. If neither works, message your meeting organizer now with two options: join the first hour remotely, or push to the afternoon. Want me to draft that message?"}
{"prompt": "How do I stop my sourdough from going flat when I bake it?", "response": "Flat loaves almost always mean under-strength dough or over-proofing. Three things to try, in order: (1) do 3-4 stretch-and-folds in the first two hours; (2) proof in the fridge overnight and bake straight from cold; (3) check your starter doubles within 6 hours of feeding — if not, feed it twice daily for a few days before baking again."}
{"prompt": "I just got a 2021 MacBook Pro with Apple Silicon but my old x86 Python scripts keep failing. How do I get everything working smoothly?", "response": "The key is using a Rosetta-independent setup. First, install Rosetta just in case: /usr/sbin/softwareupdate --install-rosetta. Then use the ARM-native Homebrew: /bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\". For Python, install pyenv (brew install pyenv) and use it to install a native ARM Python (pyenv install 3.11.4). Reinstall your pip packages fresh with that interpreter. Avoid conda unless absolutely necessary — if you must use it, get conda-forge's universal2 packages. Test with a simple import of your most critical library before migrating everything."}
{"prompt": "My dog just ate a couple of grapes. He's a 25-pound terrier. Should I be worried?", "response": "Yes, grapes and raisins can cause acute kidney failure in dogs, and there's no established safe amount — even small ingestions can be dangerous. Take action now: (1) call your vet or the ASPCA Animal Poison Control Center (888-426-4435) immediately; (2) note the time of ingestion and approximate number of grapes; (3) do NOT induce vomiting unless told to by a vet, as aspiration risk can be higher than benefit; (4) bring your dog to an emergency clinic if your regular vet isn't available. Early IV fluids are the standard treatment and work best when started within 6–12 hours."}
{"prompt": "I'm trying to learn guitar but my fingers hurt after 10 minutes of practice. Am I doing something wrong?", "response": "Pain beyond mild discomfort is a signal — you're likely pressing too hard or using poor technique. Try this: (1) check your grip — you only need enough pressure to make the string contact the fret cleanly, not crush it; (2) keep your thumb centered on the back of the neck, not wrapped over the top; (3) use a lighter string gauge (try .010s instead of .011s or heavier); (4) do two 10-minute sessions instead of one 20-minute one to build calluses gradually; (5) if pain persists beyond a week or feels sharp/burning, see a professional — tendonitis from guitar is real and preventable."}
{"prompt": "What's the best way to batch-cook meals for the week without everything tasting soggy on day 3?", "response": "The secret is separating components that get soggy and reheating smart. Follow these rules: (1) keep sauces, dressings, and wet toppings in separate containers until assembly; (2) for grains, undercook rice/pasta by 1 minute — it'll finish cooking when reheated; (3) roast vegetables on a wide sheet pan (crowding = steaming) and store them dry; (4) use airtight glass containers and cool food to room temp before refrigerating; (5) when reheating, add a splash of water to grains and microwave uncovered for the first minute. Pro tip: Tuesday/Wednesday meals should be your simplest reheated dishes; save fresh-assembling meals for later in the week."}
{"prompt": "I keep getting rejected from jobs. My resume looks fine and I'm qualified for the roles. What am I missing?", "response": "Let's audit this systematically. Most candidates miss one of three things: (1) ATS optimization — your resume must mirror keywords from the job description, not just be \"qualifying\"; use the exact phrasing they use; (2) quantifiable impact — replace duties with achievements: instead of \"managed a team,\" write \"led 6 engineers to ship feature X, reducing churn 18%\"; (3) referral strategy — 70% of roles are filled through referrals. Find 2nd-degree connections at target companies on LinkedIn, request a 10-minute intro call, then ask if they'd be comfortable referring you. Want me to review your resume line by line against a specific posting?"}
